## Direct Stack

Direct connection with no CDN in the path — lower latency and higher throughput
when the server IP is reachable. Three protocols are available; they operate
independently and clients can use any combination.

---

### Hysteria2

UDP-based protocol that disguises traffic as QUIC/HTTP3. Connects **directly**
to the server — no gateway involved. Good first choice for clients that support it.

{{HYSTERIA_STD_HEADING}}| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Domain | `{{DIRECT_DOMAIN}}` |
| Port | `8444 UDP/TCP` |
| Password | `{{HYSTERIA_PASSWORD}}` |
| Masquerade site | `{{MASQ}}` |

{{HYSTERIA_WARP_SECTION}}---

### VLESS Vision + XHTTP Reality (via gateway)

These two protocols share a `gateway-router` container (Nginx) that listens on
port 2053 and dispatches incoming connections to the Xray backend by SNI. Vision
and Reality both terminate at the same Xray process; the gateway is purely a
routing layer in front of them.

#### Gateway router

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Listen port | `2053 TCP` |
| SNI routing | `{{DIRECT_DOMAIN}}` → `vless-direct` |
| Fallback site | `{{STACK_DIR}}/gateway/www/` |

---

#### VLESS Vision (XTLS)

High-performance TLS flow. Clients connect to the gateway on port 2053 with
SNI = direct domain. Vision uses the `xtls-rprx-vision` flow to strip the inner
TLS layer for maximum throughput.

{{VISION_STD_HEADING}}| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Domain / SNI | `{{DIRECT_DOMAIN}}` |
| Port | `2053` (via gateway) |
| Protocol | VLESS |
| Flow | `xtls-rprx-vision` |
| UUIDs | `{{VISION_IDS}}` |

{{VISION_WARP_SECTION}}---

#### VLESS XHTTP Reality

TLS without a certificate — the handshake borrows the identity of a legitimate
site (the Reality target). Resistant to TLS fingerprinting because the server
presents a real certificate for the impersonated domain.

{{REALITY_STD_HEADING}}| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Port | `2053` (via gateway) |
| Network | XHTTP |
| Path | `{{XHTTP_PATH}}` |
| Reality target | `{{REALITY_TARGET}}` |
| SNI / server names | `{{REALITY_SNI_INPUT}}` |
| Public key | `{{REALITY_PUB_KEY}}` |
| Short IDs | `{{REALITY_SHORT_IDS_CSV}}` |
| Protocol | VLESS |
| Flow | `xtls-rprx-vision` |
| UUIDs | `{{REALITY_IDS}}` |

{{REALITY_WARP_SECTION}}> The Reality **private key** is stored in `{{STACK_DIR}}/reality-keys.txt`.
> Never share it — the public key above is what clients need.

